<title>PERU: Peru's June mined lead output rises 2.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's June mined lead output rises 2.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's lead output rose 2.1 percent to 21,183 tonnes in June compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures released Thursday by the Energy and Mines Ministry.</p>
<p>Lead output rose 1.7 percent to 125,000 tonnes in the first half of the year, compared with the same period last year, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Peru's lead output last year rose 4.6 percent to 248,477 tonnes from 237,597 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's number three lead producer. State-owned  Centromin is the country's largest producer of the metal.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
